  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 5.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="234" ed="#liebermann"/>Unde uisum est sapientibus omnibus, quod isti tres homines unius rectitudinis essent digni.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="5.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="74" ed="#robertson"/>Unde visum est sapientibus omnibus, quod isti tres homines unius rectitudinis essent digni.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="235" ed="#liebermann"/>Daher dünkte allen Witan richtig, dass diese drei [Arten] Menschen derselben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_5-1.lnote.de.1"/> Rechtsstrafe theilhaft würden.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Therefore it seemed right to all the witan that these three [kinds of] people should be subject to the same legal penalty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="75" ed="#robertson"/>It has therefore been determined by the whole council that these three [classes of] men shall incur the same punishment<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_5-1.robnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_5-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">anes rihtes weorðe</hi> hatte Original I Atr 4, 2. III 13, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The original had <hi rend="italic">anes rihtes weorðe</hi>; I Atr 4, 2. III 13, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_5-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">A.S. <hi rend="italic">anes rihtes weorðe</hi>, cf. I Atr. 4, 2; III, 13, 1.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
